units.scope:
Module `contract` — src/contract.ts

Purpose: this is the single shared type/constant module for the whole system. It has zero runtime logic, zero I/O, zero imports, and zero side effects — it exports only TypeScript type aliases, interfaces, and two string constants. Every other module (lint, grader-runner, adjudicator, panel, attack-harness, walker, ledger, author-agent, orchestrator, command-router, reporter) imports its shared record and seam-payload shapes from here rather than redeclaring them. The file must type-check standalone (`tsc --noEmit`) with no external dependencies beyond the TypeScript standard lib.

Write exactly this file (types/order may be reorganized, but every listed export, its name, and its shape must be present):

```typescript
// src/contract.ts — pure types + constants, no runtime logic, no imports.

// ---- primitives ----
export type Score = 0 | 1 | 2; // every grade dimension score is one of these three
export type Sha256Hex = string; // 64 lowercase hex chars, a sha256 hex digest

// ---- Part I record types (SRS §4) ----

export interface Spec {
  path: string;
  rev: string;
}

export interface GradeRecord {
  rater: string;
  model: string;
  manifest_hash: Sha256Hex;
  vector: Record<string, Score>;
  evidence: Record<string, string>; // dimension key -> "path:line" citation
  disposition: string;
  readiness: string;
  provisional: boolean;
}

export interface Finding {
  id: string;
  source: string;
  severity: string; // value drawn from a declared severity set owned by the capability that emits it (e.g. panel/attack); this module does not enumerate that set — do not hardcode a closed union here
  clause: string;
  text: string;
  replay?: string;
}

export type DispositionKind = 'resolved' | 'otherwise' | 'deferred' | 'rejected';

export interface Disposition {
  finding_id: string;
  kind: DispositionKind;
  reasons: string[];
}

export type WalkItemStatus = 'open' | 'discharged';

export interface WalkItem {
  citer: string;
  cites: string;
  status: WalkItemStatus;
}

export interface LedgerEntry {
  seq: number;
  prev: Sha256Hex;
  kind: string;
  payload: Record<string, unknown>;
  hash: Sha256Hex;
}

export interface ClosureRow {
  clause: string;
  class: string;
  falsifier: string;
  validation: string;
  gate: string;
}

// ---- R-S1: grader isolation manifest shape ----

export const GRADER_MANIFEST_METHOD = 'method/v0.4.md' as const;
export const GRADER_MANIFEST_SKILLS = 'skills/fspec-method' as const;

export interface GraderManifest {
  spec: string; // exactly `${Spec.path}@${Spec.rev}`, no other form
  method: typeof GRADER_MANIFEST_METHOD;
  skills: typeof GRADER_MANIFEST_SKILLS;
}
// R-S1: a manifest is valid iff its keys are exactly {spec, method, skills} — no prior
// grades, findings, scores, or revision intent may be present anywhere in the invocation
// context. GradeRecord.manifest_hash = sha256 hex of the canonical JSON serialization of
// this object with key order (spec, method, skills).

// ---- R-S4 / R-S5: adjudication result shapes ----

export interface AdjudicationRouting {
  route: Record<string, 'third-rater'>; // dimension key -> routing action, for nonzero disagreements
  contested_knockouts: string[]; // dimension keys where either rater scored 0
}

export interface AdjudicatedReport {
  vector: Record<string, Score>;
  disposition: string;
  readiness: string;
  contested_knockouts: string[];
  provisional: boolean;
  disposition_line?: 'WITHHELD' | 'SUSPENDED';
  cause?: string; // present iff disposition_line === 'SUSPENDED'; format `vacuous-pass:<clause>`
  queue?: 'human'; // present iff disposition_line is set
}
// R-S4: any dimension where either rater scored 0 => that dimension is in contested_knockouts,
// disposition_line = 'WITHHELD', queue = 'human', and disposition/readiness carry no printable
// text while withheld. A third-rater tie on a routed dimension also produces queue: 'human'.
// R-S5: a verified vacuous-pass report forces disposition_line = 'SUSPENDED' regardless of the
// vector's values, with the affected clause's dimension added to contested_knockouts.

// ---- R-S2: loop termination predicate shape ----

export interface LoopState {
  vector: Record<string, Score>;
  walk_items: WalkItem[];
  attack_clean: boolean;
  dual_rated: boolean;
  caps_active: string[]; // empty array means no active caps
}

export type LoopVerdict =
  | { verdict: 'CONTINUE'; reason: string }
  | { verdict: 'TERMINATE' };
// R-S2: the predicate that maps LoopState -> LoopVerdict MUST NOT reference the numeric sum
// of `vector`. TERMINATE iff: every vector value is nonzero AND dual_rated AND attack_clean
// AND every walk_items[].status === 'discharged' AND caps_active.length === 0. Any other state
// yields CONTINUE with a reason string naming the unmet condition (e.g. 'walk_undischarged').
// This module fixes the shape only; the predicate itself is the orchestrator's behavior.

// ---- Seam payload types (SRS §6) ----

export interface S_S1_CitationEdge { // fspec-lint -> walker
  artifact: string;
  cited_by: string[];
}

export type S_S2_GradeRecord = GradeRecord; // grader-runner -> adjudicator
export type S_S3_AdjudicatedReport = AdjudicatedReport; // adjudicator -> orchestrator
export type S_S4_Finding = Finding; // panel / attack-harness -> findings store
export type S_S5_WalkItem = WalkItem; // walker -> orchestrator
export type S_S6_LedgerEntry = LedgerEntry; // orchestrator -> ledger

// ---- Cross-document seams (SRS §6 mirrored rows / SRS-operator §8) ----

export interface S_O1_JourneyInvocation { // operator surface -> orchestrator
  journey: 'J-S1' | 'J-S2' | 'J-S3' | 'J-S4';
  spec: string;
  rev: string;
}

export interface RenderedReport { // orchestrator -> operator surface (S-O2)
  disposition_line: string; // full literal line, e.g. "Disposition: D-3 Specification-complete"
  readiness_line: string; // full literal line, e.g. "Acceptance readiness: BLOCKED — O-04"
  provisional: boolean;
  suspended?: { cause: string };
  body: string; // full rendered text; MUST end with disposition_line then readiness_line, in that order
}
// V-O1 / RV-S2 (render equals record): every field on a RenderedReport MUST be traceable
// verbatim to the AdjudicatedReport/LedgerEntry it cites, never independently regenerated.
// This module only fixes the shape; the reporter module owns the tracing/refusal behavior.

// ---- SRS-operator §6: conversational data model ----

export interface OperatorSession {
  commands: string[]; // raw command/question text, in the order issued
  renders: RenderedReport[]; // every RenderedReport shown this session, in order
  pending_proposals: string[]; // proposal ids (e.g. "prop-004") not yet merged or discarded
}
// RV-S1 (authority does not create capability) and RV-S2 (render equals record) are enforced
// by other modules (command-router, reporter); this module carries no logic and defines only
// the shapes those rules constrain.
```

Acceptance for this module: the file compiles standalone with no import errors, every type/interface/const listed above is exported with the exact name shown, and no runtime function, class, or I/O is present anywhere in the file.
